# Helm Best Practices

Authoritative standards for authoring and reviewing Helm charts in this repo.
Based on [Helm chart best practices](https://helm.sh/docs/chart_best_practices/).

## Chart Structure

Standard layout — do not deviate:

```
<chart>/
├── Chart.yaml
├── values.yaml
├── values-<env>.yaml      # per-environment overrides
├── .helmignore
├── charts/                # dependency charts (helm dep update)
└── templates/
    ├── NOTES.txt
    ├── _helpers.tpl
    ├── <component>.yaml   # one file per component
    └── tests/
```

## Chart.yaml

- `apiVersion: v2` always
- `name`: lowercase kebab-case, matches chart directory
- `version`: SemVer, bump on **any** chart change
- `appVersion`: quoted string, tracks the app, not the chart
- Always set `kubeVersion`, `description`, `keywords`, `maintainers`
- Pin every dependency with exact `version` and `repository`; gate with `condition:`

## Values

- Use **camelCase** for all keys (`imagePullPolicy`, not `image_pull_policy`)
- Document every value with a comment (purpose, type, default)
- Group related values under a single object (`image.repository`, `image.tag`, `image.pullPolicy`)
- Provide sane defaults in `values.yaml`; override only deltas in `values-<env>.yaml`
- Never put secrets in `values.yaml` — use `--set`, `-f secrets.yaml` (gitignored), SOPS, or external secrets
- Booleans: `true`/`false` only — never `yes`/`no`/`on`/`off`

```yaml
# ❌ BAD
image_tag: latest
enable_autoscaling: yes

# ✅ GOOD
image:
  repository: myapp
  tag: "1.2.0"           # pin; quote numeric-looking tags
  pullPolicy: IfNotPresent
autoscaling:
  enabled: true
```

## Templates

- One resource file per component; group tightly-coupled resources (Deployment + Service + ConfigMap) with `---`
- Use `{{ include "chart.name" . }}` helpers — never hardcode names
- Quote all strings that could be numeric: `tag: {{ .Values.image.tag | quote }}`
- Use `nindent`, not `indent`, to avoid leading-newline issues
- Gate optional resources with `{{- if .Values.foo.enabled }} … {{- end }}`
- Use `toYaml` for passthrough blocks (`resources`, `nodeSelector`, `tolerations`)
- Prefer `required "msg" .Values.foo` over silent defaults for mandatory inputs

```yaml
# ❌ BAD
image: myapp:{{ .Values.image.tag }}

# ✅ GOOD
image: "{{ .Values.image.repository }}:{{ .Values.image.tag | default .Chart.AppVersion }}"
imagePullPolicy: {{ .Values.image.pullPolicy }}
resources:
  {{- toYaml .Values.resources | nindent 12 }}
```

## Labels

Centralize in `_helpers.tpl`. Every resource must carry the standard set:

```yaml
app.kubernetes.io/name: {{ .component }}
app.kubernetes.io/instance: {{ .Release.Name }}
app.kubernetes.io/version: {{ .Chart.AppVersion | quote }}
app.kubernetes.io/component: {{ .component }}
app.kubernetes.io/part-of: {{ include "chart.name" . }}
app.kubernetes.io/managed-by: {{ .Release.Service }}
helm.sh/chart: {{ include "chart.chart" . }}
```

Selector labels (immutable) must be a **strict subset** of common labels — do not include `version` or `helm.sh/chart` in selectors.

## Dependencies

- Run `helm dependency update` and commit `Chart.lock`
- Do not commit `charts/*.tgz` — they are regenerated from the lock
- Gate each dependency with a `condition:` so it can be disabled

## Validation (mandatory before commit)

Run in the chart directory:

```bash
helm lint .
helm template release-name . -f values.yaml --debug
helm template release-name . -f values-prod.yaml --debug
helm install release-name . --dry-run --debug
```

CI must run `helm lint` and `kubeconform` (or `kubeval`) against rendered manifests.

## Hooks and Tests

- Use `helm.sh/hook: pre-install|pre-upgrade` for migrations, with `hook-delete-policy: hook-succeeded`
- Include at least one `templates/tests/` connection check so `helm test <release>` works
- Never use hooks for ordinary resources — they bypass normal release tracking

## Anti-Patterns

- ❌ Using `:latest` tags — pin to SemVer or digest
- ❌ Hardcoding `namespace:` in templates — let `-n` / `.Release.Namespace` drive it
- ❌ Computing names with raw string concat instead of `include "chart.fullname"`
- ❌ Embedding secrets in `values.yaml` or `ConfigMap`
- ❌ Skipping `appVersion` bumps when the app image tag changes
- ❌ Using `lookup` for logic that should be values-driven (breaks `--dry-run`)
